'''Krosulhah''' is a unique frost [[Skyrim:Dragon|dragon]] found outside [[Skyrim:Nchardak|Nchardak]] during [[Skyrim:The Gardener of Men|The Gardener of Men]].

His name means "Sorcerer Day Mind" in the [[Lore:Dragon Language|dragon language]].

{{NewLeft}}

==Related Quests==
*{{Quest Link|The Gardener of Men}}

==Dialogue==
When encountered, he hovers above the ruins and bellows before attacking you and [[Skyrim:Neloth|Neloth]].
:''"Miraak has commanded your death. So it shall be."''

He will taunt you during the battle:
:''"When Miraak returns, all will bow before him"''

:''"Soon, Miraak will return to resume his rightful {{hover|kingdom/kingship|junaar}} over Solstheim!"''

He shares several lines of dialogue with [[Skyrim:Sahrotaar|Sahrotaar]], as they are both in the faction "[[Skyrim:Combat dialogue for dragons allied to Miraak|Combat dialogue for dragons allied to Miraak]]":
:''"My thuri Miraak is the only true Dovahkiin."''

:''"{{hover|Courageous fool|Krin mey}}. You are a fool to challenge Miraak. His thu'um is supreme."''

:''"Your death has been foretold."''

:''"{{hover|Serve or die|Aam uv dir}}. Those that will not serve Miraak must die."''

If you use [[Skyrim:Dragonrend|Dragonrend]] on Krosulhah, he will comment on it:
:''"{{hover|Foul Words of Power|Bein Rotmulaagge}}! What foul Words are these?

:''"No dovah would stoop to such vile {{hover|treachery|tahrovin}}."''

Once he has landed on the ground, he will say:
:''"Now we will see whose thu'um is the stronger!"''

:''"You are strong, Dovahkiin. {{hover|Very strong|Rinik mul}}. But not strong enough."''

==Notes==
*Krosulhah is more talkative than most other dragons, taunting you throughout the fight. If you inflict [[Skyrim:Dragonrend|Dragonrend]] upon Krosulhah, he will have specific comments pertaining to that attack.

==Bugs==
{{bug|According to game data, Krosulhah is intended to be a [[Skyrim:Serpentine Dragon|Serpentine Dragon]], but instead has the appearance of a regular dragon. One result of this is that his blood textures don't match his body.|UDBP|2.0.5}}

